<title>INDIA: India RBI relaxes loans to non-bank finance firms.</title>
<headline>India RBI relaxes loans to non-bank finance firms.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) on Tuesday said banks will now be free to determine the level of credit to non-bank finance companies (NBFCs).</p>
<p>&quot;As part of the efforts to give greater operational freedom to banks, it has been decided to remove the existing overall limits of bank credit to such NBFCs as have fully complied with the requirements of registration, credit rating and prudential norms,&quot; it said in a communication to banks.</p>
<p>Lending by banks to NBFCs are now subject to ceilings.</p>
<p>Detailed operating instructions are being issued separately, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
